<description>
Emit the next 3-row band in a cyclic table of colored 3x3 sprite masks.

Input structure
The input is a 3x3 sprite lattice: sprite rows are separated by full
background rows, and sprite columns are separated by full background
columns.  Each column keeps one color across all sprite rows.

Rule
Ignoring color, each sprite row is the previous sprite row shifted one slot
left.  The output is the next shifted sprite row, recolored by the fixed
colors of the output columns.

Key insight
The colors mark the columns, while the uncolored 3x3 masks form the cyclic
sequence; after m input sprite rows, column j receives mask (j + m) modulo
the number of columns.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "3x3 sprite-mask lattice with fixed column colors and background separator rows/columns",
  "dst": "next 3-row band of the same column slots",
  "transform": "ignore color to read the cyclic mask sequence: each lower band shifts masks one slot left; emit the next shifted band and recolor each mask with its column color",
  "grid_shape": "3 rows by input width"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    input: (4*n_rows+1) rows x (4*n_cols-1) cols
    output: 3 rows x same width as input
  lattice:
    n_cols: 3-4 (number of sprite columns)
    n_rows: 1-3 (number of sprite bands in input)
    separator_rows: full-bg rows at positions 0, 4, 8, ... (every 4th row)
    separator_cols: full-bg columns at positions 3, 7, 11, ... (every 4th col from col 3)
  sprites:
    size: 3x3 binary masks
    count: n_cols distinct masks form the base sequence
    density: 4-7 filled cells out of 9
    no symmetry requirement [observed] some are symmetric, some not
    colors: each column has a unique non-bg color, fixed across all bands
    colors_used: distinct non-zero colors, one per column
  cyclic_pattern:
    band r, column c gets mask = base_masks[(c + r) % n_cols]
    each subsequent band is the previous shifted one slot left
  output_rule:
    output = band n_rows (the next band after the last input band)
    column c gets base_masks[(c + n_rows) % n_cols] colored with column c's color
    no separator rows in output; separator columns preserved

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (constraints are easily satisfied constructively)
  steps:
    1. Pick n_cols in [3,4] and n_rows in [1,3]
    2. Pick n_cols distinct non-bg colors
    3. Generate n_cols distinct 3x3 binary masks with density 4-7 each
    4. Build input grid of size (4*n_rows+1) x (4*n_cols-1) filled with bg
    5. For each band r in [0..n_rows-1], column c in [0..n_cols-1], place base_masks[(c+r)%n_cols] colored with color[c] at row offset 1+4*r, col offset 4*c
    6. Build output (3 rows) using band index n_rows with same cyclic rule
  mask_generation: |
    Randomly fill 3x3 grid with density d in [4,7].
    Reject if duplicate of a previously generated mask.
```
</generation_spec>
